  "title": "Repeated Pre-Vote round at the same hypothetical vote counts a delayed grant from a removed node; RaftCore panics",
  "cause": "Rounds started at an unchanged vote probe the same (term+1, self); the PreVoteResponse gate correlates by leader id only, and handle_pre_vote_resp calls grant_by for any granted response, which panics for a node outside the new round's quorum set.",
  "trigger": "Round A over {0,1,2}; node 1's grant is delayed; node 1 is removed from the voters; round B is started at the same vote over {0,2}; node 1's round-A grant arrives within the RPC timeout.",
  "consequence": "RaftCore panics ('target not in quorum set') and the node stops serving, in debug and release builds.",
  "sites": [
    "openraft/src/core/raft_core.rs:does_pre_candidate_vote_match",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:handle_pre_vote_resp",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:pre_elect",
    "openraft/src/proposer/candidate.rs:grant_by"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "ExternalPreElect",
    "HandlePreVoteResponse",
    "AppendJointConfig",
    "AppendUniformConfig"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "PreVoteGrantsWithinFrozenVoters"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "Two Pre-Vote rounds can be started at an unchanged vote (explicit triggers, or timer re-issue).",
    "A membership change can remove a responder between the rounds.",
    "Vote/pre-vote RPC responses can arrive up to election_timeout_min after sending."
  ],
